Under `--modular-termination` (https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/211), the part of the standard library that verifies with no unchecked premise can now be built as a recorded library: `dafny build --target:lib Source/DafnyStandardLibraries/modular-termination/dfyconfig.toml` (or `make build-modular-termination`), loaded with `--library` in place of the bundled standard library.  It covers the arithmetic, collections, wrappers, relations, functions, Base64, BoundedInts, DynamicArray, Math and Unicode base modules; modules with axioms, assumptions or externs, and the modules that import them, are left out.  When the bundled standard library is rejected under the option, the error now names this library.  Nothing changes without the option.
